      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is the process where a single cell divides into two genetically identical daughter cells, essential for growth and repair. This complex division is broken down into distinct stages: prophase, where chromosomes condense; metaphase, where they line up at the cell's equator; anaphase, when sister chromatids are pulled apart toward opposite poles; and finally, telophase, where new nuclear envelopes form around the separated chromosomes. Cytokinesis usually follows, physically splitting the cytoplasm to complete cell division.",
